  "releaseHighlights": "- Halation: fixed a thin dark line that hugged the edge of blown\n  highlights with the Roadshow model. The glow now peaks right at the\n  highlight edge and falls off smoothly; the color and reach of the\n  halo band are unchanged.\n- New Halation Test Chart checkbox (Textures group): replaces the input\n  with a synthetic scene-linear chart — a stop ramp into a fully blown\n  super-white plateau plus partial-highlight and warm patches — so you\n  can see exactly how your current halation settings respond.\n  Diagnostic only; uncheck before rendering.\n- Windows and Linux: Emulsion grain is now computed at the same stage\n  of the film pipeline as the Mac renderer. Grain no longer renders\n  noticeably heavier than on Mac at the same settings.\n- Textures editor: checking a module's master box while its format\n  dropdown still read \"Off\" left the dropdown and the active values\n  disagreeing; the check now lands the dropdown on its first real\n  gauge.",
