      "releaseHighlights": "- Film Stock Editor: dye curves you sculpt now survive closing and\n  reopening the editor exactly as drawn. Previously the chart came back\n  as a flattened approximation of what you drew, and the first drag\n  afterwards could visibly jump the image.\n- Windows and Linux: the Roadshow halation model now matches the Mac\n  renderer — no more dark punch-out over strong highlights, and spread\n  settings below one pixel render instead of switching halation off.\n- Windows and Linux: Emulsion grain is now computed in its own pre-pass\n  ahead of the main kernel, the same speed path the Mac renderer uses.",
